  "description": "Issue #18 sprint 4 contract evidence: booting the default (single-enabled-locale, en) modern debug ROM from a genuinely blank (all-0xFF) SRAM chip never shows the blocking first-start language selector. src/bmsave-lib.c's BuildCurrentExpansionSaveMeta() (called from EraseSramDataIfInvalid()/InitGlobalSaveInfodata() at the very start of AgbMain, before ExpansionLanguageMenu_RuntimeInit ever runs) already stamps a fully VALID default ExpansionUserPrefs record into any SAVE_COMPAT_EMPTY image -- a deliberate, already-tested (scripts/modernize/tests/test_save_format_tool.py) issue #18 sprint 2 design decision, documented in docs/localization.md. gExpansionLanguageMenuProbe (gExpansionLanguageMenuProbe (resolved from the exact ELF)) confirms: prefsState=VALID (0x05), promptShown=0, active=0, autoSelected=0 -- the resolver silently applies the stored (default en) locale with no visible UI, at both an early and a long-run checkpoint. Uses only the health/safety+Nintendo+IS logo skip presses (SKIP_HS) -- no further input is needed or given, since APPLY_ONLY never blocks on anything.",
